the calculated diffusivity reaches approximately:Charge-equilibration rateFraction of the fast-exchange diffusivity0.01 s−10.01\ {\rm s^{-1}}0.01 s−14.6%1 s−11\ {\rm s^{-1}}1 s−170%100 s−1100\ {\rm s^{-1}}100 s−199.6%The source’s carrier-capture estimates make a fast regime plausible near midgap in 3C-SiC, but they use representative capture cross sections rather than a measurement of this exact transition at the proposed annealing condition. The finite-rate calculation exposes the required input: a specific charge transition slower than roughly the structural rates could substantially reduce the effect.I have not transferred room-temperature charge-control demonstrations in 4H-SiC into a claim of acquired charge control in 3C-SiC at 1,2001{,}2001,200 K.The antisite intermediate does not become a large inventory trap in this modelUsing its published charge-dependent formation energies, and counting the available intermediate configurations, I obtainPintermediatePVV≃5.9×10−6\frac{P_{\rm intermediate}}{P_{VV}}
\simeq5.9\times10^{-6}PVV​Pintermediate​​≃5.9×10−6at the baseline mobility maximum.The equilibrium population and entry flux imply a mean intermediate residence of approximately2.1×10−5 s.2.1\times10^{-5}\ {\rm s}.2.1×10−5 s.These values are calculations within the specified model. They show that the proposed route does not require a large population to sit indefinitely in an inaccessible chemical state.The symmetry of the two exits is also useful: charge changes inside that intermediate do not, by themselves, select the forward exit over the return exit. The model pays for that return probability.The omitted charge states do not justify a spectacular free gainThe +2+2+2 state has a particularly low published barrier for one pivot. It would be misleading to assign that state unit occupancy and combine it freely with the most favourable negative-charge motion.Instead, I bounded the omitted populations using the formation-energy envelope. Near the chosen operating point, their total statistical weight is at most about 3.5×10−53.5\times10^{-5}3.5×10−5 of the retained +1/0+1/0+1/0 weight under the baseline energy assumptions.A rare state can nevertheless contribute appreciably if its barrier is sufficiently low. Allowing an arbitrarily fast complementary pivot, while retaining the acquired silicon-pivot rate, caps the diffusion coefficient at approximately4.5×10−21 m2 s−1.4.5\times10^{-21}\ {\rm m^2\,s^{-1}}.4.5×10−21 m2s−1.Thus the omitted channel could strengthen the baseline prediction by a factor of a few. It cannot support an unlimited enhancement by neglecting the cost of occupying its charge state.Activation entropy remains a consequential inputThe source calculates appreciable, pathway-dependent thermal corrections, but does not supply all the charged-path free energies required here. Its neutral silicon-pivot barrier decreases by about 0.370.370.37 eV between zero temperature and 1,5001{,}5001,500 K. A common prefactor therefore cannot establish an accurate experimental clock. link.aps.orgThe transport geometry and the exact diffusion formula survive that uncertainty. The location, magnitude and useful temperature range of the mobility window require the corresponding free energies. Those quantities should be acquired together; independent fitted rate curves would weaken the construction.5. One appealing application fails in the same chemical settingThe calculated divacancy diffusivity exceeds the isolated silicon-vacancy diffusivity near this window. That initially suggests selective removal or relocation of divacancies while leaving silicon-vacancy qubits in place.That interpretation fails when the competing chemistry is included.At the same 1,2001{,}2001,200 K, EF−EV≃1.16E_F-E_V\simeq1.16EF​−EV​≃1.16 eV condition, the published silicon-vacancy-to-carbon-antisite-vacancy pathway gives a baseline conversion rate of approximatelykVSi→CAV≃0.71 s−1,k_{V_{\rm Si}\rightarrow CAV}\simeq0.71\ {\rm s^{-1}},kVSi​→CAV​≃0.71 s−1,or a characteristic time of about 1.4 seconds. This calculation uses the source forward barriers and charge populations, rather than inferring chemical survival from a low diffusion coefficient.Consequently, isolated silicon vacancies would not simply remain as stationary qubits while divacancies moved over hours. They would change chemical identity.This is a physical failure of that proposed selective-purification operation. It is stronger than saying that an experiment has not yet been performed.The surviving operation is narrower: control the mobility of an already assembled divacancy population, with competing species and loss reactions treated explicitly.6. What the strongest realised alternatives already accomplishThe comparison prevents an inflated invention claim.Charge-assisted formation is established. Lühmann and colleagues reported NV-centre creation yields up to 75% in diamond, with improved spin coherence, using donor-assisted charge control to favour formation and suppress competing defects. Their work includes evidence of vacancy charging. A generic proposal to improve defect assembly by Coulomb attraction or repulsion would not be a new enabling operation. Nature CommunicationsFeedback-controlled placement is also a strong incumbent. Laser processing with fluorescence feedback has already written individual NV centres at selected locations with near-unity yield. A proposed atomic-manufacturing method must therefore offer something beyond producing an emitter somewhere in a prescribed region. arxiv.orgConventional SiC annealing is effective. A 2025 experimental study found its strongest divacancy-related emission after annealing 4H-SiC at 1,2731{,}2731,273 K, consistent with a useful separation between precursor migration and divacancy migration. Those observations concern another polytype and do not directly measure the transport coefficient calculated here, but they are a substantial practical benchmark. researchgate.netFinally, the broad principle that charge changes can lower defect-migration barriers is prior science. Transition-state redox calculations explicitly address it. NPG Asia MaterialsThe potentially useful contribution here is more specific:A bound complex can acquire translational mobility by exchanging between electronic states that favour different, individually confining atomic motions. Its mobility must be calculated on the connected spatial reaction network.The 44-fold result does not mean that a new treatment would outperform an existing anneal by 44-fold. A real anneal may already contain these charge-exchange events. It means that a charge-preserved description of an entire composite migration can miss a substantial contribution.7. The constructive direction that survivesI would sustain this branch as electronic control of post-assembly atomic transport, with the constitutive result preceding a device claim.The material capability worth pursuing is the separation of two operations:Assemble a useful atomic motif.Allow or suppress translation of that motif through its internal reconstruction paths.The present calculation supplies a concrete mechanism for the second operation and predicts a discriminating response: a mobility maximum near a charge-state crossover, with much less transport away from that window.It does not yet supply a destination. Uniformly increasing diffusion broadens a written pattern; it does not position it. A spatially varying electrical potential, a physically justified capture site, or feedback would have to provide that additional control. Their forces and charge populations must enter the same free-energy model as the migration pathways.There is likewise a distinction between choosing doping for one anneal and repeatedly switching the mobility of the same sample. The former is compatible with established processing. The latter still needs a demonstrated electronic control interface at the required temperature.The useful foundational lesson is already concrete: local rearrangement rates do not determine transport until their spatial cycles and state-changing connections are included. Here the crystal supplies the repeated geometric reference, and the acquired atomic pathways supply a translation cycle. That makes this a stronger physical starting point than selecting another fluxional molecule and hoping its internal motion reaches the material.The next decisive scientific question is whether the mobility window survives the complete charged free-energy and escape network with enough selectivity to support controlled relocation. The present result gives that question a specified mechanism, quantitative predictions and a clear failed application to avoid.
